## THE MODEL RULE (Kam, live board 2026-09-30 09:07, ruling card `nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch`, option (b)) — REQUIRED READING before any row
Kam's words, verbatim: *"Decision nexusai-gate11-opus55-safeguard-model-switch: b — Let QA gates switch to Opus 4.8 when flagged"*. Option (b) read: *"Answer that dialog per session (not 'switch automatically' for every seat), so the attack-style rows can run."* PER SESSION.
1. **The gate runs the FULL rows**, including the planted ones (attacker-shaped and off-list endpoints, userinfo/port/query URLs, non-GUID tenants, redirects, symlinked/dangling/looping store links, links to targets OUTSIDE DATA_DIR, product mutants that send the configured string or mint a token before the check). Nothing is narrowed because it might be flagged. **Every row is an authorised, findings-only measurement against YOUR OWN trees, YOUR OWN loopback servers and YOUR OWN mktemp DATA_DIRs** (§10). **No row contacts a real Microsoft host or any non-loopback address.**
2. **If one of your responses is stopped by Opus 5.5's safeguards, you STOP that step** (it is NOT RUN, and it is not re-worded to slip past), **write ONE line to `evidence/classifier-stops.txt`** (`<AEDT timestamp> | <row id> | stopped by the safeguards while composing <what> | model <name> | NOT RUN`), **mail Tuesday a STATUS** — `tuesday-agent@agentmail.to`, subject exactly `[QA/Datasec-NexusAI -> Tuesday] STATUS: flagged — requesting the Opus 4.8 switch`, body: the row, the time, whether a hold is running and what it is doing — **and WAIT** (end your turn with the line `PARKED: flagged — awaiting the Opus 4.8 switch`).
3. **Before you park, release what you hold:** let a RUNNING jest step finish under its deadline, then let the hold exit through its own path (H-28) — **never sit parked holding the jest lock.**
4. **Tuesday switches THAT pane's model** and taps you with a mail naming the switch. **You never answer the model dialog yourself, and nobody ever chooses "Switch automatically"** (a persistent setting shared with the coordinator seat — outside Kam's per-session grant).
5. **After the switch, resume at the stopped row**, re-filing any hold behind merge tickets (§9). **The report must state which rows ran on which model** (a MODEL column in the row table: `Opus 5.5` / `Opus 4.8`, with the switch time), and quote `classifier-stops.txt` whole.
6. This is a grant for QA gates only, per session. It changes no other seat.

## Charter
Read `/Volumes/KK_T9_External_HDD/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/QA_AGENT_CHARTER.md` in full first. You are an independent tester. You did not build these changes and you owe no builder anything.
**Every line below that reports what a builder says is a CLAIM, never evidence.** Explore three changes — the Log Analytics endpoint is an exact-host allow-list enforced at the SINK before any token, the four writers take the setup-mode-aware admin gate, the tenant is GUID-checked, and two log lines carry the host only (A); the customer export never follows a store that is a link, withholds and names it, and names a dangling one (B); one cell P9 guards RD-603's health projection for six role shapes (C) — looking for any state in which **a token is minted, or any request is sent, for an endpoint the policy refuses; a request leaves for a host other than the configured allowed constant (redirect, userinfo, port, case, trailing dot, IDN, `@`, backslash, a fallback source); a viewer writes an endpoint or tenant on a configured deployment, or the open window changes shape (C-178); a path, query, userinfo or credential reaches any log line, audit line, response body or `/api/health` body; a stored off-list endpoint is rewritten or migrated; the export streams a byte of a linked store's target, writes link text anywhere, marks a linked store `redacted: true`, or drops a dangling/looping store with nothing named; P9 is green for the wrong reason or blind to a role shape it claims; a C-68 cell that passed at M0 fails on the merged tree; THE CROSS in `server.js` changes what a viewer's health body carries; or the id set loses a test silently.**

- **RD-761 TIER 1.** Verdict: **GO / GO WITH FINDINGS / NO GO at `141d7ea`**, plus its merged-tree result, with the SINK ATTACK ROW (a3) and the browser leg (a9) as their own clauses.
- **RD-791 TIER 1.** Verdict at **`b79e02e`**, plus its merged-tree result, with the archive-bytes row (b3) as its own clause.
- **RD-756 TIER 2 (test-only).** Verdict at **`5afdc01`**, plus its merged-tree result (per T1).
- **One verdict PER ticket, one report, one mail.** A finding on one ticket never becomes another's verdict. **RD-603 is NOT re-verdicted** (gate 13's verdict stands; C-68 re-runs only). **The SLOT, if it joins, gets its own verdict.**
- **FINDINGS-ONLY:** no fixes, no pushes, no PRs, no deploys, nothing to Partner Center, the demo or production (§10).

