## 9. Floor discipline — THE FOUR CLAUSES, plus MERGES GO FIRST and THE DEADLINE RULE
1. **MERGES GO FIRST (ruling i).** **The jest lock `session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh` (queue `session-tools/locks/queue-jest/`) is shared with gates 14, 15 and 17 (`qa-b14-`, `qa-b15-`, `qa-b17-` tags, LIVE) and the builder seats** (at 14:03:41 the queue held `s87n-merge-rd671`, `qa-b14-H10`, `qa-b15-H10`, `s89r-rd794-hold07-probe`, `qa-b17-H35` — READ).
   - **Do ALL lock-free work first:** pins, reads, merge-trees in scratch objects, the offline `npm ci` (H-31), the plain-node, server and browser rows (a2-a7, a9, b2-b5, y2), census greps, prior-work reads, CI reads.
   - **Then file your holds (H-28), ONE AT A TIME**, each tagged `qa-b18-…` (e.g. `qa-b18-H1`), each a tracked child of your seat. **If a MERGE ticket (a tag containing `merge`) is queued AHEAD of you, you wait behind it (that is FIFO). If a MERGE ticket FILES BEHIND YOU BEFORE YOUR HOLD IS GRANTED, re-file your ticket behind it:** stop YOUR OWN unstarted waiter (its ancestry proven to reach your claude pid — C-174: by pid, never by pattern), confirm your ticket went to `released/` as `ticket-left-*`, and re-queue with `--after <that merge ticket's tag>` (C-141 ADDENDUM 4's tool) **under your UNCHANGED tag** (ADDENDUM 5). **At a wait deadline while FIRST in line: ruling (i)'s replace-then-withdraw.** Record each re-file with its place before and after FROM THE QUEUE LISTING (gate 16 S-6). **Once your hold is GRANTED, carry on** — a running hold is never interrupted; **between holds, re-file behind any merge ticket.** Gates 14's, 15's and 17's tickets are PEER gates': FIFO, never re-filed around, never touched.
   - C-141: your hold is gate-class; builder PROOF tickets self-apply ONE yield per gate TAG. **QUEUE, NEVER TAKE OVER:** never kill, signal, move or edit another seat's process, lock directory, owner file or ticket, even if it looks stuck; if a holder looks stuck, mail a QUESTION (§11) and keep waiting. **Known lock-tool message (RELAYED by builders):** `nexusai-lock.sh: line 241: …/nexusai-jest.lock/owner: No such file or directory` at acquire, then a normal grant — record it if you see it.
2. **Hold the lock for a planned block of work, never idle (H-28)** — at most ~40 minutes of planned jest per hold, one hold at a time. Every hold is a TRACKED CHILD of your seat, never detached (`nohup … &`).
3. **Count foreign servers the C-125 way, anchored on YOUR OWN claude pid:** `basename(argv[0]) == node` AND the server entry point anywhere in the remaining argv; "ours" = the ancestor chain CONTAINS your own claude pid. **Record the foreign count BESIDE EVERY RESULT — including every server you boot OUTSIDE a hold (a3-a7, a9, y2).** **NEGATIVE controls, all in the same run, all must classify FOREIGN: the claude pids of the LIVE cockpit panes among `Datasec/NexusAI-M`, `-N`, `-O`, `-P`, `-R` and the coordinator pane `tuesday`, DERIVED LIVE by the launcher at launch and listed at the end of your prompt** (and the claudes of gates 14, 15 and 17, if their panes are live). This brief names no pids: they change with every restart. Re-read them at the start of every hold; if one has exited, say so and use the others; **a hold with NO live negative control aborts.** Reuse gate 16's instrument BY COPY with YOUR pid as `ROOT` and these as `NEG` (`qa-floorlib16.sh`, its defaults STALE — correct `ROOT` and `NEG` before any hold) and `…/qa-floorcount.py`. Count every child you start and prove 0 left after each run (H-33).
