**5. THE DEADLINE RULE — every probe, every child and every request has a per-step DEADLINE, a HEARTBEAT, and kills its child in a `finally`.**
Each step (offline npm ci 600 s, node driver 120 s, server boot 60 s, browser arm 180 s, targeted jest 600 s, C-68 union 1,800 s, full verify 2,400 s, exit 25 s) has a written DEADLINE (`qa-to.sh`); a step past it is ABORTED and reported, never waited on. **Log a HEARTBEAT line at least every 2 minutes during any hold (H-4: a separate child, ≤ 120 s max gap, aborted if absent at 90 s); a step with no heartbeat for 5 minutes is aborted and reported,** and a hold that is not progressing releases the lock. Every process and child you start is killed in a `finally` (SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after a grace) **by pid from your own ancestry, never by pattern (C-174)**, and the reap is confirmed by your floor counter. **H-20 and H-21 apply to every jest.**

